<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>





<handout>
    <title>Learning Target 14 Practice</title>

    <p >
        <em>Negate a statement with and, or, not, implies,
                            exists, and/or for all.
        </em>
    </p>

   <paragraphs>
           <title>Need to know</title>
   
           <p>
               <ul>
                   <li>
                       <p>
                           How to negate conditional statements (e.g.
                           <q>if...then...</q> statements).
                       </p>
                   </li>
   
                   <li>
                       <p>
                           Use DeMorgan's Laws to negate statements with ``and'' and
                           ``or''
                       </p>
                   </li>
   
                   <li>
                       <p>
                           Negate statements that have ``there exists'' or ``for all''.
                       </p>
                   </li>
   
                   <li>
                       <p>
                           How to avoid the word not.
                           Like changing ``<m>n</m> is not even'' to ``<m>n</m> is
                           odd''.
                       </p>
                   </li>
               </ul>
           </p>
        </paragraphs>
   
       <paragraphs>
           <title>Practice Questions</title>
   
           <p>
               <ol>
                   <li>
                       <p>
                           Weekly Practice 10 #4
                       </p>
                   </li>
   
                   <li>
                       <p>
                           Worksheet pages 69-71
                       </p>
                   </li>
   
                   <li>
                       <p>
                           Write a useful negation of the following statements.
                           Useful negations don't start with things like ``It is not
                           true that...'' and avoid the word not when possible.
                           <ol>
                               <li>
                                   <p>
                                       There exists <m>x\in\mathbb{Z}</m> such that if
                                       <m>y\in\mathbb{Z}</m> then
                                       <m>\dfrac{y}{x}\in \mathbb{Z}</m>.
                                   </p>
                               </li>
   
                               <li>
                                   <p>
                                       For all <m>y \in \mathbb{R}</m> if <m>y\ge 0</m>
                                       then <m>\sqrt{y}\in \mathbb{R}</m>.
                                   </p>
                               </li>
   
                               <li>
                                   <p>
                                       For all <m>r\in\mathbb{R}</m>, if <m>r&gt;2</m>
                                       then <m>r^{2}&gt;4</m>.
                                   </p>
                               </li>
   
                               <li>
                                   <p>
                                       For every student in the class, if they studied
                                       and completed the homework, then they passed the
                                       exam.
                                   </p>
                               </li>
   
                               <li>
                                   <p>
                                       For every real number <m>x</m>, there exists a
                                       real number <m>y</m> such that <m>x + y = 0</m>.
                                   </p>
                               </li>
                           </ol>
                       </p>
                   </li>
               </ol>
           </p>
       </paragraphs>

        </handout>